INSERT INTO question_bank_2_examples (id, group_id, content, sequence)
VALUES (
  '6425e4d7-3e5b-5b1b-9bf0-b2ce8bb2567e', 'e4a06421-f3cf-5751-ab21-ef3da1d452c7',
  'Following is C like pseudo code of a function that takes a number as an argument, and uses a stack S to do processing.

```c
void fun(int n)
{
    Stack S; // Say it creates an empty stack S
    while (n > 0)
    {
        // This line pushes the value of n%2 to stack S
        push(&S, n%2);

        n = n/2;
    }

    // Run while Stack S is not empty
    while (!isEmpty(&S))
        printf("%d ", pop(&S)); // pop an element from S and print it
}
```

What does the above function do in general?

